ry cases.", "review": "Submit a state trace and a causal explanation of two outputs. Explain a changed input without running it first."}, "swift-m3-l1": {"trace": "Validation models either an accepted integer or a rejection reason. Item separates an immutable id from a changeable quantity. These declarations do not reject negative stock by themselves; add a validated construction or update path. A data type's shape and its business rules are related but different responsibilities.", "practice": "a stock validation result and compare copied structs with shared class instances.", "review": "Submit source and normal, empty, and invalid input results. Each stated acceptance condition must pass."}, "swift-m4-l1": {"trace": "The encoder turns Expense(amount: 20) into JSON bytes. The decoder rebuilds an Expense from those bytes, and print displays 20. A successful decode shows compatible structure, not that every amount is allowed. Reject negative amounts explicitly if the expense rules forbid them.", "practice": "a JSON import that distinguishes malformed bytes from invalid amounts.", "review": "Submit the failing case, root cause, minimal fix, and a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after."}, "swift-m5-l1": {"trace": "The actor owns value and serializes access to its isolated state. increment changes it; read returns it. This declaration makes no calls and displays nothing. From outside the actor, use the required asynchronous access. Actor isolation protects this state but does not automatically make several separate calls one atomic business operation.", "practice": "an actor-based counter and an ownership diagram for a callback retaining its owner.", "review": "Submit a comparison of two designs, evidence from tests, one limitation of the chosen design, and a reasoned decision."}, "swift-m6-l1": {"trace": "balance receives any store obeying LedgerStore. It loads amounts and adds them from zero. If loading throws, balance propagates the failure inste