 "The course document embeds two small lesson summaries and reads them together. It does not create a separate lessons collection. If lessons become large independently edited records, consider references instead. Explain who owns each update before deciding which model is easier to maintain.", "practice": "Compare embedded lesson summaries with referenced full lesson documents.", "review": "Submit source and normal, empty, and invalid input results. Each stated acceptance condition must pass."}, "mongodb-m4-l1": {"trace": "Three expense documents become two grouped documents. books totals 30 and travel totals 5; sorting by group id makes the order explicit. The pipeline reads records and does not rewrite the expenses. Running the fixture insertion twice would double the totals, so begin with a fresh collection.", "practice": "Add a category filter before grouping and trace which records remain.", "review": "Submit the failing case, root cause, minimal fix, and a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after."}, "mongodb-m5-l1": {"trace": "The index makes studentId unique in this collection. The inserted record can be found by S1. A second S1 is rejected, but the index does not by itself require a meaningful name or a particular studentId format. Add schema validation and test missing fields separately.", "practice": "Test duplicate identities and missing required fields as separate failures.", "review": "Submit a comparison of two designs, evidence from tests, one limitation of the chosen design, and a reasoned decision."}, "mongodb-m6-l1": {"trace": "The dump writes a local backup and the restore maps it to a different training database name. A changing source requires a consistency plan; these commands alone do not prove a cross-collection snapshot. Compare counts and reports after restoring, and never present an untested archive as guaranteed recovery.", "practice": "Restore fictional documents to a separate database and explain consistency limits."